speechtext:
Mr. WERMENLINGER;
1.	By whom was the king's printer requested to insert the list of registrars of electors in Canada Gazette of January 16, 1937?
2.	What w'as the date of this request?
3.	Was the king's printer requested to hold the publication of the list of registrars of electors until the month of March next?
4.	What were the actual expenses incurred in the printing of the list of registrars of electors in the Canada Gazette of January 16 last, for (a) typesetting (b) paper, presswork, overhead, etc.?
Mr. RINFRET;
1.	Dominion franchise commissioner, but no date requested for insertion;
2.	January 12th, 1937.
3.	No.
4.	(a) and (b)-cost not appreciable in amount and not susceptible of calculation in items stated.

The interchange officers from Great Britain in Canada are as follows:
Capt. and Bt. Major G. H. A. MacMillan, M.C., Argyl & Sutherland Highlanders at Royal Military College;
Capt. E. F. B. Cook, R.E., at Royal Military College as instructor in engineering;
Capt. T. C. Thompson, M.C., Royal Signallers to signal training centre, Camp Borden;
Capt. J. B. Gordon-Duff, Rifle Brigade, to
P.P.C.L.I.;
Lieut. J. S. Symons, R.H.A. to R.CA.;
Lieut. H. A Prince, Sixth Gurkha Rifles, to R.C.R.
That is a total of six, and we have also six officers interchanged with these officers, who are on various duties in England, for instance:
Major J. C. Murchie, R.C.A. at War Office;
Capt. & Bt. Major W. C. Thackray, R.C.A. to Royal Artillery;
Capt. N. J. W. Smith, R.C.E. to R.E., Aider-shot;	[DOT]
Lieut. H. F. Cotton, P.P.C.L.I. to First Battalion Rifle Brigade;
Capt. G. W. Smart, R.C. Signallers to Fourth Division Signallers;
Lieut. R. M. Crowe. R.C.R. to Fifth Battalion 12th Frontier Force Regiment, India.
This practice has been going on for many years; it is no new departure.
